```js
function buildPagoda(cx, cz) {
  const halfWs = [4, 3, 3, 2, 1];
  const wallHs = [2.4, 2.2, 2.0, 1.8, 1.6];
  let y = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    const hw = halfWs[i], wh = wallHs[i];
    // floor slab: extent hw+1, thickness 0.5
    const fe = hw + 1;
    for (let x = -fe; x <= fe; x++)
      for (let z = -fe; z <= fe; z++)
        voxel(cx + x, y + 0.25, cz + z, i === 0 ? C.stone2 : C.woodDark, { sx: 1, sy: 0.5, sz: 1 });
    y += 0.5;
    // wall ring at |x|==hw or |z|==hw
    for (let x = -hw; x <= hw; x++) {
      for (let s of [-hw, hw]) {
        const corner = Math.abs(x) === hw;
        const pillar = corner || Math.abs(x) % 2 === 0;
        addWall(cx + x, cz + s, pillar);
        addWall(cx + s, cz + x, pillar);
      }
    }
```
Wait: when x = ±hw, the loop adds both (x, s) and (s, x) → corners duplicated (x=hw,s=hw) and (x=hw,s=-hw)... (s,x) with x=hw: (hw, hw) duplicate and (-hw, hw). Also (x=-hw, s=hw) → (-hw, hw) dup. Duplicates overlap exactly — z-fight! Avoid: iterate only z from -hw to hw for the two faces x=±hw, and x from -hw+1 to hw-1 for z=±hw:

```js
for (let z = -hw; z <= hw; z++) {
  place(cx-hw, cz+z); place(cx+hw, cz+z);
}
for (let x = -hw + 1; x <= hw - 1; x++) {
  place(cx+x, cz-hw); place(cx+x, cz+hw);
}
```
place(px, pz): pillar if Math.round distance to corner: (|x|===hw && |z|===hw) or pattern: pillar when (Math.abs(x)+Math.abs(z))... simpler: isPillar = (Math.abs(x - cx) === hw || Math.abs(z - cz) === hw) && (Math.abs(x-cx) === hw && Math.abs(z-cz) === hw) → corner pillars; also mid pillars every 2: for ring positions compute u = coordinate along side; pillar if u % 2 === 0 (with hw integer, u ranges -hw..hw: pillar at even u) — corners have u=±hw (even if hw even). hw=4: pillars at -4,-2,0,2,4 ✓ nice. hw=3: -3,-1,1,3 ✓.

