Emissive windows: on cream panels at even? On side mid: for the south face (z = cz+hw? facing camera) place window instead of cream at specific spots: if !pillar && u === 1 && hw >= 2 && (side is one of four) → window color emissive. Add for u in [-1,1]? Just u===±1? For hw=3, u=-2..2: u=-1,1 cream→window. For hw=4: u=-3..3 → windows at -1,1. Tier 0 maybe door instead: south face (z=cz+hw, x=cx, u=0..? door: for tier0 south face, x in [cx-1, cx+1] at ground → replace wall with dark door color for u in -1..1? Wall height full; door look: dark voxels. Fine: tier0, side z=+hw (south), positions x = cx, cx±1 → door color '#3a2a20', skip window there.

